module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a consumer that needs a MODULE CLOSURE -- every module the subject depends on -- is answered by an import-line BFS (extract_import_paths, parse-tree import params, or an adjacency built only from ImportResolutionFact). A provider reached only by a qualified or bare reference is omitted. The compile, skip-set, regen, or fixture then proceeds over a strict subset of the one closure authority (v1_compiler.cli_run extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint: import edges PLUS dotted-reference PLUS bare-reference, to a joint fixpoint). HARM, TWO MECHANISMS, NOT ONE INCIDENT: (1) fixture/compile loaders -- unresolved-type / undefined-variable against a module that resolves in every authority-built closure (loud when the omitted provider is demanded). (2) Class B skip-set -- class_b_path_affects_gate is dag_closure.contains on an ordinary provider .dag path, and class_b_import_closure_gate_skip_label_for_ci takes the not-affected skip when no changed path intersects that set, so a provider-only modification omitted from an import-only closure can wrongly SKIP the gate. Other unconditional-run conditions may mask a particular change; they do not reverse this mechanism. No observed production false-skip incident is claimed here; the direction is the possible silent skip, not 'fails to skip'.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE. Classify by what the CONSUMER means, never by the walker's name. If the consumer compiles, typechecks, evaluates, skips, regenerates, or otherwise treats membership as 'everything this module depends on', the walk must be the one closure authority (or the v2 equivalent), never a second BFS over import lines. Closure-meaning follow-ups (not repaired in this census PR): policy_entry_closure_sources (compile_clean_unlisted_import_use_blocks_from_policy compiles and evaluates the policy Bool -- keep that caller's typed refusal; repair through the shared authority, never a whole-tree fallback), v1/tests resolve_imports_transitively, compiler_tests resolve_source_closure, the four stage0 witness bins, emit_resolve_transitively_fn. Leave as import-graph / other: project_layer_import_syntax_facts (authored import edges), the import-syntax-presence preflight, compile_entry_on_declared_import_closure_only (restricted test_hooks contract -- do not widen that hook into the full-closure question), ExclusionOrphansImporter (retained importer naming an excluded module -- that narrow diagnostic does not establish that no reference-only dependent can be orphaned). layer_import_facts is not wholly an import-only BFS: it also incorporates reference_edges_as_import_facts for import-less files. v2.lens.module_graph import_closure walks supplied edges via dependency_closure; replacing it with a live source loader would mix layers. Two hits made it a class: gunbc#13437 (resolve_virtual_source_with_imports) and gunbc#13464 (import_closure_dag_files). Both now seed from declared entries and route through extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint; #13464 keeps a test-only import-line mutant.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: this is not 'imports are incomplete'. An import line, a qualified reference and a bare reference are the SAME dependency edge in this namespace. An import-only walk is not a narrower closure but a blind one. Nor is it entry_closure_admits_modules_the_entry_does_not_use (over-closure via the bare census); this class is UNDER-closure. A walker that already calls the authority after an import-line seed (primary_root_subject_closure, regen_input_sources_over_roots, resolve_virtual_source_with_imports after #13437) is not a second authority. resolve_transitively_bfs_legacy is already named as that seed under primary_root_subject_closure; treating it as a proven omitted walker is a misclassification, not a discovery.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 2, mechanically preventable, on the two repaired production paths, with DIFFERENT evidence grains (DESIGN section 4b(1) -- do not cite the stronger path for both). #13437: emit_host fixture_closure_union_control_union builds the live witness-root module index and resolves the std.syllogism specimen through it (mandatory live-floor pair; not a small isolated tree). #13464: isolated fixture-tree RED / import-only mutant / real-error control under import_closure_dag_files_controls, retained on CI; reported mutation execution of the production skip-set is a separate claim and is not this control. THE CLASS AS A WHOLE SITS AT THE MINIMUM ACROSS ITS IN-SCOPE PATHS: remaining compile-subject loaders (policy_entry_closure_sources, v1/tests resolve_imports_transitively, compiler_tests resolve_source_closure, four stage0 witness bins, emit_resolve_transitively_fn) still answer closure with import lines. Reporting the whole class at 2 would be inflation. Honest standing of the UNREPAIRED paths is mitigatable.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Closure membership for a compile subject is decidable from the same three channels the authority already iterates; a second import-line BFS is a fork, not a missing fact. Ceiling is not 4 while the seed may still write a VecDeque over extract_import_paths.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, at capability grain: every compile-subject loader is derived from the one closure-extension authority (extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint, or the v2 producer that is that relation), so an import-line BFS cannot be bound as a compile closure. WHAT DOES NOT SATISFY IT: grepping for extract_import_paths (the scanner is legitimate for the import-graph consumers named above); routing one more call site while the emitted crate still ships resolve_transitively_with_seen; or a lens that flags BFS without naming the consumer's meaning. Completeness of the site table is the PR-body reconciliation pinned to revision 970c30c3aacb59c9e00d23b340a9c7a0a7a87759 (walker sources unchanged by this receipts edit), not an unbounded 'every walker in the tree' claim.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster. It does not retire the remaining walkers; each closure-meaning site is its own follow-up with the same RED/mutant/control shape.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
